><!----><!----><h2 _ngcontent-ng-c4119717991=3D"" class=3D"cdk-visually-hid=
den screen-reader-model-response-label ng-star-inserted"> Gemini said </h2>=
<!----><!----><structured-content-container _ngcontent-ng-c4119717991=3D"" =
class=3D"model-response-text has-thoughts processing-state-visible enable-2=
026q1-formatting-improvements ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c2203491952=3D""=
 style=3D"height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2203491952=3D"" class=3D"conta=
iner"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c2203491952=3D"" _nghost-ng-c243940496=
7=3D"" id=3D"message-content-id-r_cf190f1a2778ff34" class=3D"ng-star-insert=
ed"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2439404967=3D"" inline-copy-host=3D"" class=3D"mark=
down markdown-main-panel tutor-markdown-rendering stronger enable-updated-h=
r-color" id=3D"model-response-message-contentr_cf190f1a2778ff34" aria-live=
=3D"polite" aria-busy=3D"false" dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"--animation-duration: =
400ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node=3D"0">Asses=
sing Thad for the Advisory Board role=E2=80=94specifically to spearhead and=
 support the pre-seed raise=E2=80=94reveals a highly capable executive who =
brings significant strategic value, along with a few operational boundaries=
 that will need strict management.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">Here is a =
breakdown of why he is a strong candidate for this specific role, and where=
 the potential friction points lie.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"2"><b data-=
path-to-node=3D"2" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Strategic Fit (Why He Works=
)</b></h3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"3"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0"><b=
 data-path-to-node=3D"3,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">He Thinks Like a VC:<=
/b> During your previous discussions, Thad immediately pressure-tested your=
 financial modeling. By pushing you to increase the raise target from $1M t=
o $3M, demanding more aggressive revenue projections ($5M in Year 1), and s=
uggesting a much higher valuation cap ($30M) to prevent early dilution, he =
proved he understands the exact mechanics and scale that institutional inve=
stors are looking for in the current AI market.</p></li><li><p data-path-to=
-node=3D"3,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Exe=
cutive Credibility:</b> Having a seasoned operator with a track record of s=
caling companies and navigating high-value Series A rounds adds immediate g=
ravity to your pitch deck. Investors like to see a technical founder backed=
 by an experienced "business" sounding board.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-n=
ode=3D"3,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Found=
er Alignment:</b> He explicitly stated his philosophy is to protect the fou=
nder and execute the founder's vision objectively. This is exactly the mind=
set you want from an advisor who will be reviewing your cap table and term =
sheets.</p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"4"><b data-path-to-node=3D"4"=
 data-index-in-node=3D"0">Potential Friction Points (What to Manage)</b></h=
3><ul data-path-to-node=3D"5"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"5,0,0"><b data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"5,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The "Co-CEO" Expectation:</b>=
 Thad mentioned in his correspondence that in his advisory roles, he tends =
to operate more as a "Co-CEO" rather than just showing up for a few hours a=
 month. While his enthusiasm is great, the standard Founder Institute FAST =
agreement is designed for a low-friction, 2-to-4-hour monthly commitment. I=
f he expects to have veto power or heavy operational control for only 0.5% =
to 1.0% equity, that could cause friction.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"5,1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"5,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Cash=
 Remuneration Hurdle:</b> Previously, Thad indicated a desire for cash comp=
ensation before the funding round closed. Since paying an unregistered indi=
vidual a cash success fee for raising capital can trigger severe SEC and FI=
NRA violations (the unregistered broker-dealer trap), it is critical that h=
is compensation remains strictly bound to the time-vested equity outlined i=
n your Advisory Agreement.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0"><b da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"5,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Domain Expertise vs. Gen=
eral Operations:</b> Thad is a self-described non-technical "business guy."=
 While he understands market dynamics and scaling, he may not have the hype=
r-specific rolodex of deep-tech or AI-infrastructure venture capitalists th=
at a former AI-focused VC might possess.</p></li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node=
=3D"6"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Verdict</b><=
/h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"7">Thad is a <b data-path-to-node=3D"7" data-in=
dex-in-node=3D"10">very strong fit</b> for the Advisory Board, provided the=
 boundaries of the engagement are clearly defined.</p><p data-path-to-node=
=3D"8">He has the operational maturity to rigorously refine your Go-To-Mark=
et strategy and the financial acumen to ensure your deal terms protect your=
 equity. As long as the <i data-path-to-node=3D"8" data-index-in-node=3D"16=
7">Revised V2 Advisory Agreement</i> firmly locks in the time-vested equity=
 structure (avoiding transaction-based success fees) and clearly defines hi=
s role as strategic guidance rather than daily operational control, he will=
 be a highly valuable asset to have in your corner during investor meetings=
.</p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!=
